{"language":"python","task":"Write a Python function that takes a pre-trained deep learning model and a list of layer names as input. The function should set the weights of the specified layers in the model using a provided dictionary of weights, and then save the modified model to a file in a specified format.

    Only return the code, don't include any other information,
    such as a preamble or suffix."}

message.content:
{
    "code": "import tensorflow as tf

def set_and_save_weights(model, layer_names, weights_dict, save_format='h5'):
    for layer_name, weights in zip(layer_names, weights_dict.values()):
        layer = model.get_layer(layer_name)
        if isinstance(weights, list):
            for sub_layer, sub_weights in zip(layer.submodules, weights):
                sub_layer.set_weights(sub_weights)
        else:
            layer.set_weights(weights)
    model.save(f'modified_model.{save_format}')"
}
